cdot 2 + 1 \\cdot 1 = 8 + 0 + 2 + 1 = 11_{10}\n  \\]\n\n### Step 2: Add the decimal numbers\n\n\\[\n5_{10} + 11_{10} = 16_{10}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Convert the sum back to binary\n\nTo convert \\(16_{10}\\) to binary, we repeatedly divide by 2 and record the remainders:\n\n\\[\n16 \\div 2 = 8 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n8 \\div 2 = 4 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\div 2 = 2 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\div 2 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\div 2 = 0 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\n\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get:\n\\[\n16_{10} = 10000_2\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of \\(101_2\\) and \\(1011_2\\) in base 2 is \\(\\boxed{10000_2}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{10000_2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:321"}
